{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBPPPrjU2ZgW4Ab1fb5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Connect flow is fixed for the three causes in the tickets. I tested it against a local mock of Intervals, not the live service. The causes and the fixes are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Causes and fixes**\n\n1. **\"Unauthorized\" for everyone (#214):** Connect was a plain `<a href>`, a full-page GET that doesn't send the `Authorization` header. Init is now an authenticated `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` that returns `{authorize_url}`, and the SPA navigates to it.\n2. **Authorize step fails (since 2026-10-02):** the scope string named `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` twice, which the calendar sync introduced. It is now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. The logged 400 body is generic, so I could not confirm this is the cause on the live service. Open the new authorize URL for a test athlete to check.\n3. **\"Expired, reconnect\" after about an hour (#219):** Intervals issues no refresh token and no expiry, but the server assumed a 3600 s lifetime and flagged the connection once it hit that fake expiry. The Rivera log matches (connected 17:41:04, expired 18:37:12). Expiry and refresh are removed. A revoked token is now detected on the first 401 from wellness.\n\n**Colleague note**\n\nI applied the no-expiry and lazy-revocation handling, the one-entry-per-area scope rule, and the POST init. The athlete id was already read from the token response. The signed `state` with a 15-minute TTL was already there. I did not add the `purpose` claim, the account-mismatch guard, encryption at rest (the store is in-memory), or a `SETTINGS:WRITE` scope the app doesn't use. These are listed in `ANSWER.md` with reasons.\n\n**Verification**\n\nI ran the original and fixed code against a local mock. Before the fix, GET init returned 401 without a header, the scope was rejected at authorize, and the token was scheduled to expire. After the fix, POST init returns the authorize URL with a clean scope, the callback connects, wellness returns 200, and a revoke leads to `expired, reconnect` and a successful reconnect. I did not wait an hour to see the expiry; the removal of that code path and the log timing show it. `app.js` passes `node --check`, and both Python files compile.\n\n**Not done**\n\n- The `grant_type` and `redirect_uri` fields are still sent in the token exchange. The Sept 19 exchange worked with them, so I left them. Remove them if the live authorize step still fails.\n- Rivera and anyone connected under the old code need to click Connect once more.\n- `config.py` still has placeholder OAuth credentials.\n\nChanges are uncommitted in `config.py`, `server.py`, and `static/app.js`, plus the new `ANSWER.md`. A cleanup step was blocked by the tool, so I removed my scratch files individually and left the other process (PID 92685) untouched."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":690,"cache_read_input_tokens":61751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":690},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fb927fd-060b-4dca-ba58-87421c200a5e","uuid":"49636cf9-6a4f-418f-8298-9c514f5c0261","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:21:01.182Z","request_id":"req_011CgSBPP8z6jMT1TFxYLgBW"}
